# E §3.1 step 1: the hash is of the canonical text, "so spacing never changes a hash"; L §2.4 "The loader accepts any
# spacing that the grammar allows. It then reprints the model as follows, so equal models print identically". Member
# b is member a's text with its sections in another order, other spacing, a redundant pair of parentheses and the
# number written 0.120: both are pinned by one hash (a's canonical text), and both load.
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "ana.tally" sha256 "2d61ff780d5901933b42389a451da2ceaa7f3ab91f1506e12f0eb5b4b546304e"
  use b = "ben.tally" sha256 "2d61ff780d5901933b42389a451da2ceaa7f3ab91f1506e12f0eb5b4b546304e"

ask r: a.rate + b.rate
=== ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"

input rate: num

def twice: num = rate + rate

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  rate = 0.12 "umowa"
=== ben.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  rate = 0.120   "umowa"
def twice : num = (rate+rate)
input rate:   num
source s "umowa"
=== expect
r: 0.24
  cut 2026-10-20
